{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787405761371543001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"mid-aeronautic-wombat","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"683c3d63b314e02b1c73ff683c627562ef057c6a8aa9e6cb0c660be8bd0420d2","event_uuid":"03fe7d50-c42f-4c57-9c0e-dd0ee3e6745c","position":{"commit_sha":"fd799aadeee4becb077f994f439901a767e7119f","position":"1787400558528443001-03fe7d50-c42f-4c57-9c0e-dd0ee3e6745c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"98426e90334319a77bf8ba084cab5f849f72b0eb03feac9d6c94f5a202161597","event_uuid":"9f122199-edeb-4412-ac32-0c29ecff2464","position":{"commit_sha":"cd68d30a64ce1fd5164ebd5d4c50be7fef92775c","position":"1787400568433392001-9f122199-edeb-4412-ac32-0c29ecff2464"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787400558528443001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9f122199-edeb-4412-ac32-0c29ecff2464","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"52b0-6a6a-c66b-4c59"}],"description":"LLM-Review advisory on S10 (52b0-6a6a-c66b-4c59, Gerrit change 2104 patchset 3, doctor_mapping.py:~220). The live-drift diff treats a configured link target absent from the probe's observed set as a drift ERROR. But the probe port's issue_link_types() is fail-soft — it returns [] on any exception (mapping_probe). So a PARTIAL probe failure (link-types API errors while statuses/types succeed) yields an empty observed link set, and EVERY configured link target then appears as drift → false-positive blocking errors, without degrading to 'unavailable'. Non-manifesting on the happy path (a full transport failure degrades to unavailable before this). Fix options: (a) skip the link axis when observed link-types is empty (can't distinguish 'no link types' from 'API failed'); (b) make the probe port distinguish empty-vs-failed for link-types and fold a link-types failure into the unavailable finding. Advisory/defensive; the drift check is best-effort and never the sole gate.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0d24-0055-d8d2-4ab0","ticket_type":"bug","title":"doctor live-drift: link-axis false-positive when issue_link_types() fails soft to []","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["03fe7d50-c42f-4c57-9c0e-dd0ee3e6745c","9f122199-edeb-4412-ac32-0c29ecff2464"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787405761371543001,"uuid":"52c710c4-84a5-4e6a-82aa-57c744d74b2b"}